WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.002
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Proficiency.

2
00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:08.526
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.826 --> 00:00:19.524
Unit sixteen: Religion and Modernity. In this unit, you will discuss religion, tradition and modern society respectfully.

4
00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:21.657
secularism.

5
00:00:22.357 --> 00:00:27.248
secularism means the separation of religion from state institutions.

6
00:00:27.548 --> 00:00:30.824
Secularism takes different forms in different countries.

7
00:00:31.524 --> 00:00:34.374
Your turn. Say: secularism.

8
00:00:37.074 --> 00:00:38.284
secularism.

9
00:00:39.283 --> 00:00:40.830
religious pluralism.

10
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:47.651
religious pluralism means the peaceful coexistence of many religions in one society.

11
00:00:47.951 --> 00:00:51.112
Religious pluralism requires mutual respect.

12
00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:55.393
Your turn. Say: religious pluralism.

13
00:00:58.093 --> 00:00:59.837
religious pluralism.

14
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.281
interfaith dialogue.

15
00:01:02.981 --> 00:01:08.858
interfaith dialogue means conversation and cooperation between different religions.

16
00:01:09.158 --> 00:01:11.726
Interfaith dialogue builds understanding.

17
00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:16.054
Your turn. Say: interfaith dialogue.

18
00:01:18.754 --> 00:01:20.486
interfaith dialogue.

19
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:22.775
Theravada Buddhism.

20
00:01:23.475 --> 00:01:29.468
Theravada Buddhism means the school of Buddhism followed in Cambodia, Thailand and Sri Lanka.

21
00:01:29.768 --> 00:01:32.929
Theravada Buddhism is Cambodia's state religion.

22
00:01:33.629 --> 00:01:36.583
Your turn. Say: Theravada Buddhism.

23
00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:40.597
Theravada Buddhism.

24
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:43.060
monastic tradition.

25
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:49.034
monastic tradition means the way of life of monks and religious communities.

26
00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:52.622
The monastic tradition preserves ancient texts.

27
00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:56.903
Your turn. Say: monastic tradition.

28
00:01:59.603 --> 00:02:01.022
monastic tradition.

29
00:02:02.017 --> 00:02:03.331
ritual practice.

30
00:02:04.031 --> 00:02:08.213
ritual practice means formal religious or cultural ceremonies.

31
00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:11.732
Ritual practice marks births, weddings and funerals.

32
00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.897
Your turn. Say: ritual practice.

33
00:02:18.597 --> 00:02:20.039
ritual practice.

34
00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:22.469
sacred space.

35
00:02:23.169 --> 00:02:26.144
sacred space means a place considered holy.

36
00:02:26.444 --> 00:02:29.570
A pagoda is a sacred space for the community.

37
00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:33.502
Your turn. Say: sacred space.

38
00:02:36.202 --> 00:02:37.575
sacred space.

39
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:40.745
spiritual but not religious.

40
00:02:41.445 --> 00:02:47.508
spiritual but not religious means having spiritual beliefs without belonging to an organised religion.

41
00:02:47.808 --> 00:02:52.385
Many young people describe themselves as spiritual but not religious.

42
00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:57.317
Your turn. Say: spiritual but not religious.

43
00:03:00.017 --> 00:03:02.388
spiritual but not religious.

44
00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.673
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:03:05.973 --> 00:03:08.925
Ms. Sarah, is religion declining in the modern world?

46
00:03:10.217 --> 00:03:16.375
In some countries, yes. Be that as it may, globally the picture is far more complex.

47
00:03:17.683 --> 00:03:21.599
In Cambodia, Theravada Buddhism remains central to daily life.

48
00:03:22.883 --> 00:03:29.692
Indeed. The pagoda is a sacred space, and the monastic tradition shapes education and ethics.

49
00:03:30.983 --> 00:03:35.305
Many of my friends say they're spiritual but not religious.

50
00:03:36.617 --> 00:03:42.032
A growing trend. Suffice it to say that belief is changing rather than disappearing.

51
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:46.675
How can societies with many faiths live peacefully?

52
00:03:47.983 --> 00:03:53.538
Through interfaith dialogue and respect. Come what may, pluralism depends on listening.

53
00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:58.997
Grammar focus: Subjunctive and fixed formal expressions.

54
00:03:59.297 --> 00:04:02.388
Some fixed expressions preserve the old subjunctive.

55
00:04:02.688 --> 00:04:08.197
Be that as it may, the picture is complex. Suffice it to say that belief is changing.

56
00:04:08.497 --> 00:04:11.495
Come what may, pluralism depends on listening.

57
00:04:11.795 --> 00:04:18.009
These fixed subjunctive expressions are formal and slightly literary; use them sparingly for effect.

58
00:04:19.017 --> 00:04:22.273
Now read and listen. Faith in a Changing World.

59
00:04:22.573 --> 00:04:28.067
Sociologists once predicted that modernisation would lead to the steady decline of religion.

60
00:04:29.383 --> 00:04:34.460
Be that as it may, religion remains a powerful force across much of the world.

61
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:41.395
In Cambodia, Theravada Buddhism shapes festivals, ethics and community life.

62
00:04:42.683 --> 00:04:48.328
The monastic tradition has historically provided education as well as spiritual guidance.

63
00:04:49.617 --> 00:04:55.378
Elsewhere, secularism separates religious institutions from the state in varying degrees.

64
00:04:56.683 --> 00:05:01.643
A growing number of people describe themselves as spiritual but not religious.

65
00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:09.988
Religious pluralism, supported by interfaith dialogue, allows diverse communities to coexist.

66
00:05:11.283 --> 00:05:18.391
Suffice it to say that the relationship between faith and modernity is one of transformation rather than simple decline.

67
00:05:19.683 --> 00:05:22.417
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:22.717 --> 00:05:25.669
The separation of religion from the state is blank.

69
00:05:25.969 --> 00:05:31.700
A, secularism. B, ritual practice. C, sacred space.

70
00:05:35.717 --> 00:05:38.215
The answer is A: secularism.

71
00:05:39.717 --> 00:05:42.822
'blank that as it may, we must continue.'

72
00:05:43.122 --> 00:05:46.311
A, Be. B, Being. C, Is.

73
00:05:50.317 --> 00:05:52.525
The answer is A: Be.

74
00:05:54.017 --> 00:05:57.319
'blank it to say, the results were disappointing.'

75
00:05:57.619 --> 00:06:02.352
A, Suffice. B, Sufficient. C, Suffices.

76
00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:08.524
The answer is A: Suffice.

77
00:06:10.017 --> 00:06:12.771
Conversation between different religions is blank.

78
00:06:13.071 --> 00:06:19.708
A, interfaith dialogue. B, monastic tradition. C, religious pluralism.

79
00:06:23.717 --> 00:06:26.773
The answer is A: interfaith dialogue.

80
00:06:28.283 --> 00:06:32.512
According to the text, what did sociologists once predict?

81
00:06:32.812 --> 00:06:39.194
A, religion would decline. B, religion would grow. C, nothing would change.

82
00:06:43.183 --> 00:06:45.949
The answer is A: religion would decline.

83
00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:54.862
Now it's your turn. Part one: What role does religion or spirituality play in modern Cambodian society?

84
00:07:00.162 --> 00:07:06.144
Part two: Use one fixed subjunctive expression; describe two roles respectfully.

85
00:07:12.444 --> 00:07:28.230
Be that as it may, modern life has changed, yet the pagoda remains central. It offers ethical guidance and community, especially during festivals. Suffice it to say that Buddhism continues to shape how many Cambodians understand kindness and merit.

86
00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:31.168
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:32.183 --> 00:07:37.494
Great work today! You learned eight new words and subjunctive and fixed formal expressions.

88
00:07:37.794 --> 00:07:42.153
Today's value is respect for culture. Be proud of our Khmer culture.

89
00:07:42.453 --> 00:07:45.582
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

90
00:07:45.882 --> 00:07:49.115
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

